      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from the Relampago Ranch, founded in 1856 by José María Mora and Thaddeus Rhodes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relampago%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1884, Relampago Ranch had become a stagecoach station on the route from Brownsville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/relampago-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Relampago has long served as the first stop on the so‑called ferrocarril subterráneo for migrants.",
